From 80049b4e3be2785f8534cbc6e99db1cc55083368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 18:30:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 547/572] feat(psci): add a flag to allow PSCI calls from
 secure world

If there is only a secure OS running, allow it to call PSCI functions.
This can be used for bare-metal software or RTOS running at S-EL1, and
without anything running in non-secure world.
A new flag PSCI_CALLS_FROM_SECURE is created to enable the feature.
This feature is not supported for Aarch32 platforms, and if an SPD is
selected.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git e134db1db32ce6cb8bd3e867a4c0ec11d78dd4c4 feat(psci): add a flag to allow PSCI calls from secure world]
